    {
      "topLeftX": 105,
      "topLeftY": 614,
      "bottomRightX": 611,
      "bottomRightY": 739,
      "content": "Equation (23) shows that ε anticommutes with ρ₃. We can therefore by a canonical transformation (involving perhaps the x's and p's as well as the σ's and ρ's) bring ε into the form of the ρ₂ of § 2 without changing ρ₃, and without changing any of the other variables occurring on the right-hand side of (24), since these other variables all commute with ε. iερ₃ will now be of the form iρ₂ρ₃ = - ρ₁, so that the wave equation takes the form",
